1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,670
A payment can look ordinary on its own.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,730
The pattern appears in the relationships.

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:09,420
Corridor follows those connections,
turning a synthetic payment flag into an

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:12,830
investigation you can inspect, explain, and revisit.

5
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:19,170
FalkorDB connects three layers: transactions and shared identifiers;

6
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,510
company policies, documents, and owners; and memory from past cases.

7
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,830
The graph does the retrieval and preserves the evidence.

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,510
Remove it, and Corridor loses both
its reasoning context and its memory.

9
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:37,670
Here is the deployed workspace, running on Vercel with a Render API.

10
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:41,810
These four flags come from seeded, fully synthetic data.

11
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,890
An analyst can inspect account history, then start an investigation.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,110
Each run gets its own case and evidence trail.

13
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,190
This is a new investigation on the hosted app.

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,060
Findings arrive as server sent events.

15
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,370
The first tool checks prior cases.

16
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:00,240
The agent then chooses from fixed graph
tools, while the application records

17
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:03,570
results and citations. The model never writes Cypher.

18
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,410
The graph is an inspection surface.

19
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,290
Select a finding to highlight its cited nodes.

20
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:12,990
Orbit, zoom, or switch to a flat view.

21
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,490
Exact transfer edges are highlighted only
when the raw result identifies them;

22
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:22,300
other connections remain context. Shared devices alone do not

23
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:25,610
establish fraud. The model proposes a verdict.

24
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:30,860
Deterministic code checks it. Freeze requires
two distinct positive evidence tools

25
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:34,850
corroborating the same account. Repeating one tool is not enough.

26
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,310
Unsupported proposals and model failures require review.

27
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:42,530
The actual outcome can be Monitor, even for a planted pattern.

28
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,710
The decision stays connected to company context:

29
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:50,230
an applicable policy and its source document,
a current precedent and its author,

30
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,570
and the employee responsible for this corridor.

31
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,030
Superseded precedents are excluded. These
are fictional demonstration policies,

32
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:01,590
not regulatory advice. Why this decision opens the saved trail,

33
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,630
step by step. Technical details reveal the parameters, raw results,

34
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:11,270
and allowlisted query. A reviewer can inspect what the tool returned

35
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,790
instead of relying only on the model's explanation.

36
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:16,670
Now a different account: mule zero.

37
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:20,780
Its first lookup retrieves the earlier
collector case, through the graph's case

38
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:25,000
membership relationships. The exact
earlier case identifier appears in the raw

39
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:28,170
result. This was verified across separate investigations.

40
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:32,410
Memory survives the conversation because it lives in FalkorDB.

41
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:37,010
Corridor also exposes twelve read tools over MCP.

42
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:41,620
It brings connected-data investigation,
agent memory, and company context

43
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:44,610
into one workspace. All data is synthetic;

44
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:49,270
no real funds are frozen. Explore the deployed app and public source.

45
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,010
This narration uses an AI-generated OpenAI voice.
